rs of  makeup and prosthetic work to play the  titular character as did Shaq Reggie  Miller and Nate Robinson one of the  unique challenges for the movies makeup  artist was to ensure that the makeup  didn't fall right off the actors faces  during the basketball scenes one of the  year's funniest gross-out comedies went  all out for its most disgusting gag for  a scene involving communal projectile  vomit the special effects team got the  cast to actually puke well sort of they  made a smoothie like concoction of fake  vomit the actors then spit it out  through tubes attached to their mouths  Pixar might have turned the entire world  towards computer animation but  traditional forms of animating haven't  disappeared stop-motion isn't going  anywhere  early man made by the team best known  for Wallace and Gromit  use claymation to bring prehistoric  times to life a team of 23 model makers  brought 273 puppets to life with each  individual puppet taking more than 10  weeks to make Wes Anderson's second  stop-motion feature  following the masterful fantastic mr.  Fox was equally eye popping and even  more ambitious than his earlier film  while fantastic mr. Fox had about 370  puppets they're working with 1105  puppets in Isle of Dogs many of the  puppets were covered in fur which  provides a unique challenge to  stop-motion animators  it makes it harder to replace the  four-legged characters facial  expressions  fracture defects the special effects  team behind much of West world season  two did a stellar job this year  among their most impressive feats we're  the drone hosts Maeve's grizzly neck  wounds and a samurai host who lost part  of his head  [Music]  this year ariana grande elevated both  her songs and the music videos that  accompanied them to a whole new level  this was especially evident in the music  video for her hit song no tears left to  cry in the music video she rotates  around a spinning hallway to pull this  off they actually built a massive  rotating corridor in addition grande  also had to get a life cast done so they  could create multiple masks of her face  some of it of course he's a little bit  of computer-generated wizardry  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you

